{
	"title": "Espace : orthogonalité, trouver le paramètre",
	"description": "Déterminer m pour que deux vecteurs, ou deux droites (AB) et (CD), soient orthogonaux (pièges : signe, z oublié, xC oublié)",
	"grades": ["T_SPE"],
	"points": ["TSPE-069", "TSPE-074", "TSPE-078", "TSPE-084"],
	"theme": "Géométrie",
	"domain": "Orthogonalité et distances dans l'espace",
	"subdomain": "Orthogonalité",
	"level": 2,
	"status": "draft",
	"delay": 90,
	"shared": {
		"cleanCoefficients": true,
		"blankDefaults": {
			"acceptDecimal": true
		}
	},
	"variations": [
		{
			"statement": "Dans l'espace muni d'un repère orthonormé, on considère les vecteurs $\\vec{u}\\begin{pmatrix}{{u1}}\\\\{{u2}}\\\\{{u3}}\\end{pmatrix}$ et $\\vec{v}\\begin{pmatrix}m\\\\{{v2}}\\\\{{v3}}\\end{pmatrix}$, où $m$ est un réel.\n\nDétermine $m$ pour que $\\vec{u}$ et $\\vec{v}$ soient orthogonaux.\n\n$m=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "u1",
					"expression": "1..4;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "u2",
					"expression": "-5..5"
				},
				{
					"name": "u3",
					"expression": "1..5;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "v2",
					"expression": "-5..5"
				},
				{
					"name": "v3",
					"expression": "-5..5"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["u2*v2+u3*v3 != 0", "v2 != 0 || v3 != 0"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:-(u2*v2+u3*v3)/u1}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"$\\vec{u}\\perp\\vec{v}\\iff\\vec{u}\\cdot\\vec{v}=0$, avec $\\vec{u}\\cdot\\vec{v}={{if:u1>1|{{u1}}}}{{if:u1< -1|{{u1}}}}{{if:u1==-1|-}}m+{{u2;()}}\\times{{v2;()}}+{{u3;()}}\\times{{v3;()}}={{if:u1>1|{{u1}}}}{{if:u1< -1|{{u1}}}}{{if:u1==-1|-}}m{{eval:u2*v2+u3*v3;+}}$.",
					"${{if:u1>1|{{u1}}}}{{if:u1< -1|{{u1}}}}{{if:u1==-1|-}}m{{eval:u2*v2+u3*v3;+}}=0\\iff \\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{ m={{eval:-(u2*v2+u3*v3)/u1}} }$"
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "Dans l'espace muni d'un repère orthonormé, on considère les points $A({{ax}}\\,;\\,{{ay}}\\,;\\,{{az}})$, $B({{bx}}\\,;\\,{{by}}\\,;\\,{{bz}})$, $C({{cx}}\\,;\\,{{cy}}\\,;\\,{{cz}})$ et $D(m\\,;\\,{{dy}}\\,;\\,{{dz}})$, où $m$ est un réel.\n\nDétermine $m$ pour que les droites $(AB)$ et $(CD)$ soient orthogonales.\n\n$m=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "ax",
					"expression": "-3..3"
				},
				{
					"name": "ay",
					"expression": "-3..3"
				},
				{
					"name": "az",
					"expression": "-3..3"
				},
				{
					"name": "w1",
					"expression": "1..3;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "w2",
					"expression": "-3..3"
				},
				{
					"name": "w3",
					"expression": "-3..3"
				},
				{
					"name": "cx",
					"expression": "-3..3"
				},
				{
					"name": "cy",
					"expression": "-3..3"
				},
				{
					"name": "cz",
					"expression": "-3..3"
				},
				{
					"name": "dy",
					"expression": "-4..4"
				},
				{
					"name": "dz",
					"expression": "-4..4"
				},
				{
					"name": "bx",
					"expression": "{{eval:ax+w1}}"
				},
				{
					"name": "by",
					"expression": "{{eval:ay+w2}}"
				},
				{
					"name": "bz",
					"expression": "{{eval:az+w3}}"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["w2*(dy-cy)+w3*(dz-cz) != 0"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:cx-(w2*(dy-cy)+w3*(dz-cz))/w1}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"$(AB)\\perp(CD)\\iff\\overrightarrow{AB}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{CD}=0$, avec $\\overrightarrow{AB}\\begin{pmatrix}{{w1}}\\\\{{w2}}\\\\{{w3}}\\end{pmatrix}$ et $\\overrightarrow{CD}\\begin{pmatrix}m{{if:cx>0|-{{cx}}}}{{if:cx< 0|+{{eval:-cx}}}}\\\\{{eval:dy-cy}}\\\\{{eval:dz-cz}}\\end{pmatrix}$.",
					"${{if:w1>1|{{w1}}}}{{if:w1< -1|{{w1}}}}{{if:w1==-1|-}}{{if:cx==0|m}}{{if:cx!=0|(m{{if:cx>0|-{{cx}}}}{{if:cx< 0|+{{eval:-cx}}}})}}+{{w2;()}}\\times{{eval:dy-cy;()}}+{{w3;()}}\\times{{eval:dz-cz;()}}=0\\iff \\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{ m={{eval:cx-(w2*(dy-cy)+w3*(dz-cz))/w1}} }$"
				]
			}
		}
	],
	"testSpecs": [
		{
			"description": "v0 : m = 1/2",
			"variationIndex": 0,
			"variables": {
				"u1": "2",
				"u2": "-1",
				"u3": "3",
				"v2": "4",
				"v3": "1"
			},
			"answers": ["\\frac{1}{2}"],
			"expected": {
				"status": "correct"
			}
		},
		{
